      "role": "user",
      "content": "That’s very evocative. I love the imagery of the \"instinctive script of survival\" and the idea of humans being \"entwined with the cycles.\" It really captures that sense of a people living within a predetermined, natural rhythm.\n\nI noticed you added a note about the second hall being a \"leap\" rather than just a distinction. That’s interesting. From a museum storytelling perspective, if we are presenting this as an evolutionary progression of human capability, doesn't that \"leap\" imply that the \"Scientific Vanguard\" represents the point where humanity truly stepped out of the animalistic/biological sphere and into a higher state of conscious agency? \n\nHow would you phrase the transition between these two experiences to make it clear to the audience that the shift from \"instinctive harmony\" to \"reasoned mastery\" isn't just a change in lifestyle, but a fundamental advancement in the human cognitive experience?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
